<binaryimage arch="V850:LE:32:RH850">
<!--
    Noelo-Lab/kuna#1629: the RH850 system-register banks.

    On RH850 the second word of LDSR/STSR carries a selID that picks one of
    the banks of 32 system registers; V850E2M has one bank and other names in
    it (register 11 is SCCFG there and FPEC here, and SCCFG moves to selID 1).
    The language V850:LE:32:RH850 is the V850 spec plus those banks, so plain
    V850E2 code under V850:LE:32:default keeps its decode
    (kuna-rh850-instructions.xml #45).

    Stage: P2 decode table (SLEIGH spec fix, no option).  The bytes are the
    output of GNU as 2.43.1 for `ldsr r6, regID, selID` and
    `stsr regID, r10, selID`; the names are those of the RH850G3K and
    RH850G3MH software manuals.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1000">
e62f2000e61f2008e65f2010e6072028e6172030e6f72038e2574008e5574008
e7574010e5574000eb574000eb574008
</bytechunk>
</binaryimage>
